1
00:00:00,855 --> 00:00:03,079
This video is for the system admin.

2
00:00:03,079 --> 00:00:09,495
You will learn how to add users, set roles and permissions, take backups, and check the system setup.

3
00:00:09,946 --> 00:00:13,086
Sign in with the admin account, and open Users.

4
00:00:17,693 --> 00:00:24,262
This list shows every account: the role, the branch, the department, and for doctors, the linked doctor.

5
00:00:24,262 --> 00:00:30,073
A warning shows doctors without an account, because their requests skip the doctor approval.

6
00:00:30,524 --> 00:00:37,193
To add a nurse: tap New user, write the name and password, choose the role Nurse, and tap her clinics.

7
00:00:37,193 --> 00:00:40,004
She will see these clinics in her requests.

8
00:00:40,455 --> 00:00:47,136
Each role has its own fields. A doctor has the linked doctor name. Procurement has a department:

9
00:00:47,136 --> 00:00:50,825
dental or dermatology. A branch manager has a branch.

10
00:01:24,386 --> 00:01:27,061
Tap Save. The account works right away.

11
00:01:27,061 --> 00:01:32,686
Passwords are saved encrypted, and every user can change their own password later.

12
00:01:33,137 --> 00:01:40,036
Roles and screens: for each management role, tap Edit and tick the permissions it gets. For example:

13
00:01:40,036 --> 00:01:46,867
reports, follow-up, complaints, or the survey. The server checks these permissions on every action.

14
00:01:47,319 --> 00:01:54,949
Backups: a full copy of the sheet is taken every night automatically. Tap Backup now before any big change.

15
00:01:55,399 --> 00:02:00,846
System setup runs by itself after every update, and shows the result of each step.

16
00:02:00,846 --> 00:02:04,499
If a step fails, you see why, and you can run it again.

17
00:02:28,736 --> 00:02:34,876
That's it. Keep only active accounts, and give each role only what it needs. Thank you!
